{"id": "EUVD-2026-59442", "enisaUuid": "6cee73a2-f61b-3257-a974-516049dfef8f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: codecs: hdac_hdmi: Validate written enum value\n\nhdac_hdmi_set_pin_port_mux() uses the written enum value to index the\ntexts array before calling snd_soc_dapm_put_enum_double(), which validates\nthat the value is within the enum item range.\n\nAn out-of-range value can therefore make the driver read past the texts\narray before the helper rejects the write. Move the lookup after the helper\nhas accepted the value.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:31", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/216336418c007c4b44c650acf2fd3d2de5bb81e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc464a6a9e352daa17b1636c090cf3185710b9a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8cbf24714d6b3f553fc959632c9781176a73a9a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f02e9064b6f84e7f93c72f134306271eb4f7de4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9131e4b023e0db5764680034bdc94aeae0b0f33d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8961b5c7889b6ecc00f1409d36826df1665df27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b08baeccdcf52fad328ad645f5b4fbee04eea34"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gpjf-6x9p-w663", "CVE-2026-74295"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06c342e1-23de-33b7-8f3b-2fdc4a3c3d1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4a3478debf36c0aa0cf0860daec245b13cd4448f <bc464a6a9e352daa17b1636c090cf3185710b9a0"}, {"id": "09e0c928-f3e0-3e28-921a-d4c997332d83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "0a1f5997-d18a-37f9-aaf1-26da733d719e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "152507d6-959b-38fd-a31d-5cf9666e6753", "product": {"name":